// Title: Hypervisor Enforced Paging Translation Disabled
// Sigma ID: 7f2954d2-99c2-4d42-a065-ca36740f187b
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2024-07-05 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685
// Description: Detects changes to the "DisableHypervisorEnforcedPagingTranslation" registry value. Where the it
//   is set to "1" in order to disable the Hypervisor Enforced Paging Translation feature.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/standa_t/status/1808868985678803222
//   - https://github.com/AaLl86/WindowsInternals/blob/070dc4f317726dfb6ffd2b7a7c121a33a8659b5e/Slides/Hypervisor-enforced%20Paging%20Translation%20-%20The%20end%20of%20non%20data-driven%20Kernel%20Exploits%20(Recon2024).pdf
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_deviceguard_hypervisorenforcedpagingtranslation_disabled.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey endswith "\\DisableHypervisorEnforcedPagingTranslation" and RegistryValueData =~ "DWORD (0x00000001)"
